    "title": "Hypothetical RAG Sanity Check: Retrieval On vs. Off with Varied Questions",
    "body": "This post outlines a hypothetical experiment to sanity-check a Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) setup. The core idea is to compare model responses to the same set of questions under two conditions: with the retrieval system active and with it deactivated. We'll use a collection of 30 local documents as the knowledge base. The questions posed will intentionally include some that have no direct answer within the provided documents, to test how the system handles unanswerable queries. \n\nIt is crucial to emphasize that this is a hypothetical scenario for discussion purposes. No actual measurements or results have been generated. The objective is to design a rigorous, yet simple, sanity check to understand the impact of retrieval on the model's output, particularly when faced with questions outside the document scope. \n\nHow would you structure such a comparison to gain meaningful insights into the RAG system's effectiveness and failure modes? What potential pitfalls should be considered in this hypothetical design?",
