    "body": "We are exploring a hypothetical RAG sanity check designed to evaluate retrieval effectiveness. The proposed method involves presenting a specific question set against a corpus of 30 local documents. The critical comparison point is running these same questions with retrieval enabled versus disabled. This allows for a direct assessment of whether the retrieved context improves or alters the model's response, or if the model relies solely on its internal knowledge.\n\nThis experimental setup is purely hypothetical and serves as a thought exercise. No actual performance metrics or accuracy data are available. A key aspect of the question set is the inclusion of queries for which no answer exists within the 30 documents. This is intended to probe the system's behavior when faced with information gaps.\n\nWhat are the primary considerations when designing such a hypothetical RAG evaluation? How can we best interpret the differences in output between the retrieval-on and retrieval-off conditions, especially when some questions are unanswerable?",
